sapphire: going back to a flip buffer gives the plane its linear format registers back

0403 restores the plane's linear registers (SRC2_ADDR, YSTRIDE1, SRC_FORMAT, UNPACK, OP_MODE, UBWC_STATIC_CTRL,
FETCH_CONFIG) when a linear frame of a surface follows UBWC ones. A frame of the copy path goes the other way, through
planeUnscaled(), which restores only the geometry and the scaler: the plane read the linear flip buffer as UBWC. Seen on
the phone after a while at rest, with the pool full and frames of surfaces outside it copied: SRC0 0x5c000000, stride
4320, SRC_FORMAT 0x800237ff, unpack 0x03010002, UBWC_STATIC_CTRL 0x121 -- lines over the screen. planeUnscaled() now
restores them too; the saved registers and the plane's state move to file scope, shared by both paths.

---
diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
index 7d8d339..3fa7cfe 100644
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
@@ -3261,6 +3261,15 @@ sweet_plane_wait(AppleCLCD *fb)
